# License

This repository is licensed layer by layer. The full license texts are in the
`LICENSES/` directory.

| Material | License | File |
|---|---|---|
| Specification text, `schema/taxonomy.yaml`, `schema.json`, examples | **CC0-1.0** | `LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt` |
| Documentation, governance, and contribution documents | **CC-BY-4.0** | `LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt` |
| Reference implementation (**not in this repository**) | **AGPL-3.0-only** | `LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt` |

## Why the specification uses CC0

The first requirement of a standard is **zero friction**. Any attribution, patent,
or compatibility clause makes another implementation choose to establish a competing
standard; a standard that requires a lawyer to adopt is really just a product
brochure.

## Why the reference implementation is not CC0

The reference implementation will evolve for a long time and needs to prevent
"fork it and offer a closed-source hosted service". It uses AGPL-3.0-only. That
license is reserved for a future implementation repository; this repository does not
contain the implementation.

## Contributions

Specification text and examples submitted to this repository are licensed under
CC0-1.0; documentation is licensed under CC-BY-4.0. Submitting a contribution means
you agree to this. See `CONTRIBUTING.md` for details.
